<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matilda of Hainaut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1293–1331</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Mahaut of Hainaut</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matilda of Hainaut was princess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> from 1313 to 1318, the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-of-villehardouin">Isabella of Villehardouin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florent-of-hainaut">Florent of Hainaut</a> and the last of the Villehardouin line. Married to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-of-burgundy">Louis of Burgundy</a>, she was later deprived of the principality by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capetian-house-of-anjou">Angevins of Naples</a> and died in captivity in 1331.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matilda-of-hainaut.jpg" alt="Matilda of Hainaut" width="320" height="149" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matilda_of_Hainaut_coin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
